      "output": {
        "message": "A couple of practical things can help break that loop: 1. **Do a quick brain dump.** Grab a piece of paper and write down whatever is running through your head about tomorrow—tasks, things to remember, or specific concerns. Getting them out of your head and onto the page lets your brain know they're safely stored and can wait until morning.\n2. **Reset outside of bed.** If you've been lying awake for more than 15 or 20 minutes, get up. Sit somewhere dimly lit and do something low-key until you actually feel drowsy, so your mind stops associating the bed with problem-solving. Writing things down is usually the easiest first step to take some of the pressure off.",
